    "lawCode": "Add Art XXIII, §1 of Chap 154 of 1921",
    "lawSection": "Port Authority of New York and New Jersey",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6623\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 154 of the laws of 1921, relating to the port\nauthority of New York and New Jersey, in relation to military leave for\nall represented and non-represented persons employed by the port author-\nity of New York and New Jersey\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide the rights and benefits provided under New York State Mili-\ntary Law section 242, to employees of the Port Authority of New York and\nNew Jersey.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Provides Definitions\n\nSection 2 Provides Leave of absence for Port Authority of NY & NJ\nemployees while engaged in performance of ordered military duty\n\nSection 3 Provides Leave of absence for Port Authority of NY & NJ\nemployees while attending service schools or training\n\nSection 4 Provides employment rights for Port Authority of NY & NJ\nemployees. Protecting them from diminution of time service, increment,\nvacation, or holiday privileges, or any other right or privilege, by\nreason of such absence, or be prejudiced, by reason of such absence,\nwith reference to continuance in office or employment, reappointment to\noffice, re-employment, reinstatement, transfer or promotion.\n\nSection 5 Provides Port Authority of NY & NJ employees pay for military\nduty, while going to and returning from such duty, not exceeding a total\nof thirty days or twenty-two working days, whichever is greater, in any\none calendar year and not exceeding thirty days or twenty-two working\ndays, whichever is greater, in any one continuous period of such\nabsence. Furthermore it provides every Port Authority of NY & NJ employ-\nee who served in a combat theater or combat zone of operations as docu-\nmented by a copy of his or her DD214, certificate of release or\ndischarge from active duty, or other applicable department of defense\ndocumentation, his or her salary or other compensation as such for any\nand all periods of absence while utilizing any healthcare related\nservices related to such duty, not exceeding five working days, in any\none calendar year. Section 6 Provides Port Authority of NY & NJ rights\nand sets contribution amounts under retirement systems\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nProviding Port Authority employees these benefits would provide parody\nbetween them and all other New York State public officers and employees,\nwhich include every person, by whatsoever title, description or desig-\nnation known, who receives any pay, salary or compensation of any kind\nfrom the state or a municipal corporation or any other political subdi-\nvision thereof, or who is in any department of the state or in the\nservice of any public authority. An oversight in the implantation of\nMilitary Law 242 has excluded employees of the Port Authority of New\nYork and New Jersey from these important rights and benefits.\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal notes at the end of the bill.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect upon the enactment into law by the state of\nNew Jersey of legislation having an identical effect.\n",
